{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1225837-alternate-inanimae-rules","id":1225837,"title":"Alternate Inanimae Rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-08T04:05:46-07:00","id":1225837,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Alternate Inanimae Rules?","content":"So the Inanimae rules we have are rather incomplete... to the point were it would have been more helpful to save them for later rather then include them in this halfbirthed form... I hope they at least flesh them out with another supplement because as is the Slithers are not very good/functional, especially for PCs.<br /> <br /> Now the Walking Away from Arcadia Podcast has a take on doing the Inanimae so that instead of Silvers to represent their unique Fae Powers they use Alternate Elements. The link to the pdf is <a href=\"https://wwarcadia.blogspot.com/2017/11/inanimae-playing-at-hearts_1.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. What do you think about this? This may be the way to go for me rather than the incomplete Slivers. They mention in Dark Age Fae the Inanimae are the ones who taught mages Weaving, so it is really weird that they literally can't Weave and only Unleash. Not to mention the Nightmare issues of only Unleashing...<br /> <br /> The other option is the Inanimae: the Secret Ways original rules, but I need to read my copy, probably up next in my queue after the Boggans book or maybe after the Dark Age Fae Book.<br /> <br /> But I would appreciate opinions on this from anyone?<br /> <br /> Does anyone else have Inanimae Houserules? Or homebrewed Phyla? The Phyla given seem more like the most common Phyla, especially for the Ondine, since they only represent Water Elementals of the Fresh waters, like they were banished from the Oceans. I feel Oceanic Inanimae would also exist. Not to mention Meteorite Inanimae shouldn't be Glomes but their own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T07:46:44-07:00","id":1225871,"title":"","content":"Honestly I've mostly been using Secret way mechanics with minor updates(They have access to unleashing, some of the phyla changes). Slivers have distinct levels. Inanimae Realms require bunks of the appropriate element is generally how I go with it and swap out the Mannikin flaw since I find that makes no sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for other phyla: If you can start breaking up water into Fresh/salt/etc you probably have room to break up Plants into different varities there. As for Meteors Its both a neat idea but I'm unsure how many there would be.<br /> <br /> As for my thoughts on potential other Phyla: There's always the Empire of Flickers. They've been referenced all over as a secret, Knockers have seen fairies in machines on the internet etc in various books so I'd like to see that developed.<br /> <br /> My other idea would potentially be a Glome variant but one that I think might have some fun unique setups: Fossils. I am not sure how I'd do this but Fossils are pretty and unique and seem like the sort of thing that might attract a fairy soul, but I'm not sure how it would effect it.. I don't think they'd properly be theirown empire but something that makes Glomes different..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T08:56:02-07:00","id":1226472,"title":"","content":"I don't have too much of a problem with the Inanimae as presented in C20. Yes, they're minimalist, but I think the only major problem is that they gain a point of Nightmare for EVERY spell they cast. I get that's a balancing factor so people don't just Unleash endlessly because it's so powerful, but I also like the idea of Inanimae only Unleashing - as reminiscent of an older, more pure form of chaotic fae magic. <br /> <br /> I think that the only change really needed is to state that Inanimae don't gain a point of Nighmare for Unleashing <i>unless</i> they botch the roll (or roll a 10 on an existing Nightmare dice) and to really work the complications when they fail to control it. <br /> <br /> That said, the options you linked do look like a fun alternate set of rules if you wanted something more complete?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/187-beccatoria","name":"beccatoria","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T02:39:38-07:00","id":1228237,"title":"","content":"Its not minimalist in a good way. You can tell they were obviously given a summerized powerset due to wordcount.<br /> <br /> I'm reading the Inanimae book now, and I am wondering its 1st ed so is it going to be easier to translate these powers, even though some are redundant to Fae Cantrips, into C20 level? It might be more satisfactory for me to just go with the linked Inanimae Realm patch instead.<br /> <br /> And Inanimae are supposed to be really subtle, and that isn't really what only being able to unleash is for. Perhaps if we ported the rules of Coaxing being a subtle type of Unleashing that's only for chimerical effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or another thought, what if the Inanimae use the Alchemies of the Hsien? That would incentivize more Hsien content. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But the book is from so far back that they conflate Mer with Ondines. Which is odd because the Merfolk refer to Nymphs, which are probably Inanimae.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And I am thinking we could have a Thallain/Dauntain type of Inanime made from Trash, and Radioactive crap, or maybe cursed bogs (that links somewhat to the idea posted in another thread for Mushroom Inanimae). Or maybe even Inanimae whose Anchors are Corpses! I like that! Corpses as Anchors! Mummies!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T06:23:14-07:00","id":1228270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1225837-alternate-inanimae-rules?p=1228237#post1228237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not minimalist in a good way. You can tell they were obviously given a summerized powerset due to wordcount.<br /> <br /> I'm reading the Inanimae book now, and I am wondering its 1st ed so is it going to be easier to translate these powers, even though some are redundant to Fae Cantrips, into C20 level? It might be more satisfactory for me to just go with the linked Inanimae Realm patch instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The vast majority of Phylla cannot use Kithain arts only Mannikins can so having some level of redundancy isn't an issue in my mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or another thought, what if the Inanimae use the Alchemies of the Hsien? That would incentivize more Hsien content. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to stop you right there.... there isn't a metal phyla(yet?) and Air Alchemy wouldn't make sense with the Wu Xing<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I am thinking we could have a Thallain/Dauntain type of Inanime made from Trash, and Radioactive crap, or maybe cursed bogs (that links somewhat to the idea posted in another thread for Mushroom Inanimae). Or maybe even Inanimae whose Anchors are Corpses! I like that! Corpses as Anchors! Mummies!<br /> </div> </div> </div>Why do you want to make everything unplayable!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T10:19:04-07:00","id":1228323,"title":"","content":"I didn't read it that Inanimae can only ever use Unleashing. I just read it as 'for now, freestyle their powers with Unleashings'. It was more about not including space for the full Slivers than it was making a point about Inanimae not being able to use cantrips with Realms and levels.<br /> <br /> My solution would be to use the old Slivers, if you have the book, or use Unleashing (without incurring Nightmare) until a future book covers the Inanimae. The old Slivers work fine, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T13:32:43-07:00","id":1228368,"title":"","content":"Technically Glomes count metal as one of their possible anchors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T15:25:37-07:00","id":1228395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1225837-alternate-inanimae-rules?p=1228368#post1228368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically Glomes count metal as one of their possible anchors.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They aren't a separate Phyla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T16:52:14-07:00","id":1228414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1225837-alternate-inanimae-rules?p=1228395#post1228395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They aren't a separate Phyla.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t say they were otherwise I wouldn\u2019t have said glomes. But there are supposed to be a lot of different phyla then the ones in the book. Like I may have Rusalka and yuki-onna as their own phlya or mash them into others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T18:11:30-07:00","id":1228433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1225837-alternate-inanimae-rules?p=1228414#post1228414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn\u2019t say they were otherwise I wouldn\u2019t have said glomes. But there are supposed to be a lot of different phyla then the ones in the book. Like I may have Rusalka and yuki-onna as their own phlya or mash them into others.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I considered Yuki-onna as an inanimae but... then basically thought that made them unplayable or at least SIGNFICANTLY limit their playability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T21:34:43-07:00","id":1228497,"title":"","content":"Phyla Homunculi of the Empire of Bones.<br /> <br /> I'm contemplating their birthrights and thinking maybe some sort of interact with the dead birthright, and I'm not sure for the other one. Maybe give them the ability to learn Slivers and Arts like Mannikins, but I could instead make an Osseus Sliver that touches on some Necromancer Shaman themes?<br /> <br /> We need a book that covers and revises the Inanimae because it would be nice to see how the Phlya within the same Empire interact, like if we had Glomes interact with a metal phylum of Jing. In fact shouldn't we have something like a Kingdom between Phylum and Empire? Like Kingdom is the Element of the Empire, and is composed of different Phyla. Also stuck on the idea of why not have Slumbering Inanimae actually in their Empires. That way the Empires are constantly populated by dreaming Inanimae. Otherwise it seems empty during the Interregnum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T00:31:42-07:00","id":1228516,"title":"","content":"Also it seems Perosemes aren't usually Krofted but new ones are born Krofted. Otherwise how do you explain an Anchor being turned into a Wind Chime? They are often Clouds or mountaintops or even more perplexing things like Trade winds. Similar concern with the Solimonds, as they mention Lighting is an option... At least with them they can be balefire. But they also mention things like Firepits would be Gladelings, which is weird I would imagine they would be Krofted, but they mention things like Ovens and advanced tech being the first Solimond Krofted. Though I would imagine Lamps being their first Krofted.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also its odd the Inanimae are the only Fae/Gallain that essentially have access to their own version of Arcadia... cept the Solimonds...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T02:15:06-07:00","id":1228532,"title":"","content":"And right now even if we had cantrips for Slivers there are only five of them. We don't have really very many ways of portraying Powerful inanimae, especially if all elders have the same powers. So what ways can we expand their potential powerset?<br /> <br /> They could get access to something like an arch Sliver power that goes past 5.<br /> <br /> They could introduce slivers based on different Elements, like my proposed Sliver of Bone.<br /> <br /> They could create slivers based on combinations of elements, such as Pyros and Petros making something like Volcanus. This has potential, and can lead to maybe the idea of slivers coming together to not so much be slivers anymore but, whole. They could be something like fragments, and need certain competency in other slivers to learn. Eventually they build up higher and higher into some sort of godlike powerset maybe.<br /> <br /> Maybe Slivers not based on Elements? Or possibly they are just rare slivers. Like maybe an Umbras that was the powerset of Inanimae of Shadow, their anchors being shadows, or hidden tombs and thus were extremely vulnerable if discovered, as light could destroy them. Maybe tie it to spirits too with Shadow touching upon Etherial qualities, and even the spirit world. And Astros a sliver of the Stars. Or a Flicker empire sliver based on electricity and light.<br /> <br /> Maybe some sort of Metaslivers not based on elements, like how Kraina have Genus Loci, or the Arts have Contract. So maybe a sliver of change, or a sliver of naught? Or a Fossil Phyla sliver based on Giant Beasts or the Past?<br /> <br /> We need more ways express Inanimae's power, and unlike Hsien their Splinters aren't very all encompassing, like sphere magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T04:50:20-07:00","id":1228546,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of combining Slivers. It seems very appropriate. I'd also let them use Arts and let them using the coaxing rules for Unleashing, which were published in an early preview of C20. It feels more appropriate that they can better control their Unleashings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T13:26:18-07:00","id":1228664,"title":"","content":"I like the idea there are Glomes and then the are &quot;Fossil glomes&quot; or &quot;metal Glomes' Like how there are three castes of Assamite. In this.. I'm going to say something really crazy. I kind of want the Corpse Inanimae to be the same Empire as Manikins its their dark secret.. the Empire of dolls used to be the Empire of bones but there are FAR more dolls than mound corpses..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T13:48:45-07:00","id":1228670,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about that too. Before thinking of an Osseus sliver I was thinking they would work like Mannikins with their powers. I mean if you were anchored to human bones you would have a connection the other gladlings didn\u2019t have to meat and humans in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T13:50:44-07:00","id":1228672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1225837-alternate-inanimae-rules?p=1228670#post1228670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about that too. Before thinking of an Osseus sliver I was thinking they would work like Mannikins with their powers. I mean if you were anchored to human bones you would have a connection the other gladlings didn\u2019t have to meat and humans in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Remember too that Mannikin are the element of &quot;spirit&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T01:47:38-07:00","id":1229322,"title":"","content":"We need more discussion in books about what Slivers mean. They talk about it being part of the greater power of the Fae of Old, but not every Fae was omnipotent. It sounds more like a sliver of Godhood or Omnipotence, rather then a Sliver of each Fae.<br /> <br /> Also what about Slivers for Brand New Phyla, like maybe a Datum Sliver for Computer/AI phyla? It wouldn't be a sliver of the old power of the fae would it?<br /> <br /> I would like maybe a sliver for each of the Elements representing the subtle and abstract qualities that shadow an Element. Like<br /> <br /> <b>SLIVER IDEAS:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Flux</b> for Pyros, since they mention fire wroughts change.<br /> <br /> Stasis/Morphus for Petros as the Earth is about form and permanence.<br /> <br /> <b>Ktisis/Dimiourgia/Chaos</b> for Verdage, basically the Creation birth aspect of plantlife.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Aionios</b> for Aquas, since the splinters associated water with time just make a splinter about time and eternity.<br /> <br /> <b>Apeiron</b> for Stratus since the Splinters associated air with space, have a splinter dedicated just to space/indefinition/chaos.<br /> <br /> Others:<br /> <br /> <b>Osseus</b> for the missing element of Bone, for the Homonculus Inanimae, perhaps as suggested it represents a primordial precursor to the Mannikins as an aspect of spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Thanatos</b> could be the subtle variant of Osseus, representing Death and even the other worlds of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <b>Datum</b> could be a new Sliver from those born of the nascent Empire of the Machine. It could represent purpose and Knowledge like those from a purposely created machine, the manipulations of simple machines, and even recorded data.<br /> <br /> <b>Logos</b> could be the subtle Sliver for Datum, representing Order, Intent, Reason, and consciousness.<br /> <br /> <b>Splinters of the Heart Question</b><br /> <br /> Maybe for the Heart question we could also include some secret Slivers Inanimae seek to master. Maybe the Heart question could represent the Inanimae's version of the Siochain.<br /> <br /> <b>Eros</b> being the heart of the heart question. Love, especially as known by humanity is a divine secret the Inanimae often would give quite a lot to find out. Thus their version of Golconda could have a sliver harnessing it, which naturally also includes Anteros, hate. But this isn't the blunt art that was Aphrodisios that got converted and cannibalized into Summer. This would also represent want, and possibly even hope.<br /> <br /> <b>Gnosis</b> would be the splinter that could possibly represent the missing piece of the divine, and purpose that the heart question could fulfil.<br /> <br /> <b>Agon</b> would be the Splinter known well to the mortal heart, perhaps even more then Eros. Suffering is something rocks may not be naturally familiar with but to seek the Heart Question you must learn the suffering of a man's heart. <br /> <br /> <b>Deimos</b> and finally the splinter representing dread. Like the other three Heart Question Splinters, dread and loss are not something Elemental beings were necessarily born with, but it cuts at the heart of the issue. To know man is to know the potential for loss. For Fear. Pinnochio may never have found the blue faery at the end if he did not truly have it in him to fear loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T23:44:54-07:00","id":1230473,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Okay I'm on the Splinters section of the Secret Paths book, and I plan to Read Dark Age Fae after this. But they mention Slivers are supposed to be complimentary as the Slivers make up one whole. So I'm thinking what if the Slivers that you learn can be merged somewhat, like mage spheres. So if you have Petros 1 Living Rock, and Verdage 1 Solarium you can use them both in conjunction to not just change rocks into other minerals, but change rocks into vegetation. This fits well with the original idea of what Slivers are supposed to be that never got realized in the book. With enough combinations of Slivers you could create living stones with properties of plants, maybe if their is a sliver that can animate things. Also just to get this straight, Inanimae can only learn the level 5 of their Elements Slivers right? And Mannikins can't learn level five in any Sliver or Art? So if I design more slivers I maybe any Phyla that connects to that element should be able to master it?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T02:48:24-07:00","id":1230485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1225837-alternate-inanimae-rules?p=1230473#post1230473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Also just to get this straight, Inanimae can only learn the level 5 of their Elements Slivers right? And Mannikins can't learn level five in any Sliver or Art? So if I design more slivers I maybe any Phyla that connects to that element should be able to master it?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I am pretty sure they can learn level 5 of their sliver and their complimentary slivers but not their counter sliver. But that might just be something stupid that came up in Larp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T22:50:36-07:00","id":1252969,"title":"","content":"Yeah, only Mannikins can't go to 5, other Inanimae can go to 5 in anything available to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""}